{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_015CNJErLmRgzKAfngbySP9a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Summary â€” Deliverables session: `anchor_gui.py`\n\n**Goal / what this deliverable is**\n- `anchor_gui.py` is Anchor's primary interface: a self-contained local HTTP dashboard server (stdlib only â€” `http.server`, `json`, `socket`, `threading`) that serves an interactive dashboard and writes every change directly to the markdown files, logs it, and refreshes state (file docstring, lines 1â€“14).\n\n**Key structure / components**\n- **Paths & safety:** Data paths resolve through the shared `paths` helper honoring `ANCHOR_DATA_DIR`; all markdown/JSON mutations are serialized behind a process-wide `WRITE_LOCK` so concurrent `ThreadingHTTPServer` requests can't lose an update (lines 23â€“47, `_with_write_lock` at 5004).\n- **Markdown parsing â†’ data:** `parse_tasks_from_md`, `parse_projects_from_md`, `parse_inbox_from_md`, `parse_archived_tasks`, and `gather_all()` (reads DASHBOARD.md + domain files, dedups tasks) load markdown into Python dicts (lines 181â€“388).\n- **Change operations:** `mark_done` / `mark_undone`, `add_task`, `capture_inbox`, `link_task`, `edit_task`, `edit_project`, `cancel_task`, `save_for_later`, `restore_task`, with `log_change` recording activity (lines 5013â€“5439).\n- **HTML generation:** `generate_html()` builds the entire dashboard (embedded CSS/JS) as one string (line 5439); `render_project_window_html` (the large R&D \"cockpit\" project window, lines 2209â€“4765) renders lane tiles, the kanban, grass workbench, and cost/rollup sections.\n- **HTTP server:** `AnchorHandler(BaseHTTPRequestHandler)` (line 7453) dispatches GET `/` and the many `/api/*` and `/api/rnd/*` endpoints.\n\n**R&D control-surface features present in the file**\n- A hand-rolled stdlib **WebSocket** codec (`ws_accept_key`, `encode_text_frame`, `decode_frames`, lines 464â€“635) carries ConPTY terminal bytes for live sessions.\n- **Traversal-safe static asset routes** for the vendored anchor-term, xterm, and Ghost World Labs brand mark (`anchor_term_asset`, `xterm_asset`, `brand_asset`, lines 660â€“752).\n- **Project lifecycle / summaries:** `open_project_instance`, `create_new_folder_project` (with `_maybe_git_init`), `discover_and_adopt`, plus background-summary triggers `_trigger_project_summary` / `_trigger_session_summary` and the continue-seed builder `_build_continue_seed` (lines 752â€“1075).\n- **Dashboard reflection (v6):** `_project_activity_reflection` + `render_project_tile_html` render per-project status dot, cached objective summary, and a \"what's happening\" activity line (lines 1203â€“1388).\n- **Grass workbench:** `_render_grass_column_tile`, `_render_grass_workbench`, `_render_grass_idea_li` render the two-pane idea workbench (lines 1767â€“1894).\n- **Deliverables lane:** `ensure_anchor_deliverable` pins `anchor_gui.py` as the Anchor deliverable; `render_deliverables_html` renders the lane (lines 4874â€“5004).\n\n**Server lifecycle / single-instance guard**\n- `_ExclusiveThreadingHTTPServer` + `make_server` bind `127.0.0.1:8777` with an exclusive-address guard so a duplicate Anchor process exits cleanly instead of squatting the port; `resolve_bind_host` and a `_heartbeat_watchdog` round out the boot path (lines 9578â€“9741).\n\n**Findings / honest notes**\n- No run-execution metrics are present in the member document itself â€” this is the source file, so claims above are grounded in code structure (function/class definitions and the module docstring), not in a captured run log.\n- The bulk of the file (â‰ˆ2,200â€“4,765) is the single large `render_project_window_html` cockpit renderer, consistent with the documented note that its JS lives in a raw single-brace string, not an f-string."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2197,"cache_read_input_tokens":62079,"cache_cre